1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,178
AI agents can now build Oracle APEX apps in APEXlang.

2
00:00:04,438 --> 00:00:06,889
The hard part is getting every property right.

3
00:00:08,039 --> 00:00:12,122
A single KPI card is about seventy lines of nested source.

4
00:00:12,382 --> 00:00:16,206
Every guessed name or wrong nesting costs another compile round.

5
00:00:17,356 --> 00:00:20,969
So APEXREST ships a library the agent reads offline.

6
00:00:21,229 --> 00:00:23,745
Pinned Oracle references define the grammar.

7
00:00:24,005 --> 00:00:30,951
A component catalog covers 109 families with 176 compiler-checked recipes.

8
00:00:31,211 --> 00:00:34,132
Pattern recipes show how components work together,

9
00:00:34,392 --> 00:00:38,957
and 1,350 public Oracle pages serve as references.

10
00:00:40,107 --> 00:00:43,647
The agent searches in plain words, in English or Ukrainian.

11
00:00:43,907 --> 00:00:47,510
Ready recipes rank first, and the top hit carries its code.

12
00:00:47,770 --> 00:00:52,117
Responses stay under 7 KB, with at most three lookups per change.

13
00:00:53,267 --> 00:00:55,980
A recipe is a contract, not just a snippet:

14
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:59,967
the data it expects, the names to adapt, working APEXlang,

15
00:01:00,227 --> 00:01:02,779
and compiler evidence bound to a checksum.

16
00:01:03,929 --> 00:01:08,216
The agent adapts it to your page: item names, SQL and columns.

17
00:01:08,476 --> 00:01:11,921
Then the real Oracle compiler checks the whole application.

18
00:01:12,181 --> 00:01:16,194
A typo returns its file, line, column and the valid values.

19
00:01:16,454 --> 00:01:19,103
One targeted fix, and validation passes.

20
00:01:20,253 --> 00:01:24,196
One ship call plans, backs up, imports and verifies the change.

21
00:01:24,456 --> 00:01:27,905
And the labels stay honest: ready means it compiles offline.

22
00:01:28,165 --> 00:01:31,709
SQL, import and browser checks are recorded separately.

23
00:01:32,859 --> 00:01:36,540
Less guessing. Grounded APEXlang. Verified changes.

24
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:39,156
APEXREST, for Codex and Claude Code.

